{"n": 150, "w": 1000, "h": 764, "img": "150.webp", "text": "1165020 REMOVING AND INSTALLING\nTURBOCHARGER\n\nThe turbocharger receives oil from the engine\noil circuit. The following points are important\nto guarantee sufficientlubrication for the fast\nrunning turbocharger.\n\n— Engine oil circuit in pertect condition\n(specified engine oil, oi! level, crankcase\nventing, etc.).\n\n~ Engine not raced before building up engine\noil pressure (control lamp) — engine also not\nstopped at high speed (turbocharger keeps\non running).\n\n~ Engine not started immediately after an oi!\nchange, but instead oil pressure built up\nfirst by cranking engine with the starter\n(fuel shutoff electric lead disconnected —\nsee 11 00 039).\n\nExcessively old engine oil could cause\ncarbonization of the turbocharger. Carbon-\nization could be seen on the turbocharger\nshaft after removing the oil pipe. In this\ncase the engine oil and oil filter have to be\nreplaced,\n\nImportant When Working on Turbocharger:\n\nEven the most minute particles of dirt could\nlead to destruction of the turbocharger —\ntherefore never operate engine without the\nair filter,\n\n~ If the hose on the control valve is discon:\nnected, this could lead to overcharging and\ndestruction of the engine when operated in\nfull load range.\n\nThe turbocharger may not be repaired.\n\nRemove air cleaner\nDisconnect hoses (1 and 2)\nUnscrew nut (3) and remove air cleaner housing\n\nUnscrew exhaust pipe on turbocharger\nDisconnect hoses (1 and 2).\n\nUnscrew nuts (3).\n\nfastatlation:\n\nReplace self-locking nuts.\n\nCheck gasket, replacing if necessary.\nCoat studs with copper paste “CRC\"**\nTightening torque’.\n\nUnscrew oil pipes (1 and 2).\n\nJastallation:\n\nReplace seals.\n\nTightening torque*.\n\nCheck engine oil level, correcting if necessary.\n\nUnscrew bolts and remove turbocharger\nInstallation:\n\nCheck levelness of sealing surface.\nTightening torque*\n\n* See Specifications\n** Source of Supply: HWB", "word